It's faster to use matrix for calculation, so you can convert your list into the following matrix and do the calculations you need. In your case, you can use colSums function to get the number of appearance of each string "V1" to "V8".
             V1, V2, V3, ...    , V8
row_01    1,   1,   1, ...    , 1
row_02    1,   0,   1,  0, ..., 0
 .
 .
 .
row_length(dm)

